    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113-a33">

                <pb facs="0292" n="220" xml:id="pg220"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 32 in No. 331.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Barrows to Mr.
                            Lowell</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Dublin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-01-30"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 30,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On the 23d instant James White applied to
                    me by letter for protection as an American citizen, he having been arrested
                    under the coercion act and confined in Naas jail. I wrote White on the 25th,
                    asking him to produce proof that he was an American citizen, and this morning
                    received his naturalization paper, which I have now the honor to transmit,
                    together with two letters written me by White.</p>
                <p>Awaiting your instructions,</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>B. H. BARROWS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
